WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.160
Wassup, yo?

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:18.400
This week on Thug Notes, we gettin ice cold with "Wuthering Heights" by Emily Brontë.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.380
So some fool, Lockwood, arrives at Thrushcross Grange,

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.440
a pimpin manor across the way from another phat crib called Wuthering Heights.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.480
After meeting his emo landlord, Heathcliff,

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.940
Lockwood hits up the maid, Nelly, and asks her to tell him what went down in this hood.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:38.400
Back in the day, the top dawg of Wuthering Heights, Mr. Earnshaw, picked little Heathcliff off da street,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.680
and decided to raise him as his own.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:46.440
At first, Earnshaw’s two legit kids, Catherine and Hindley, can’t stand Heathcliff’s freeloadin ass!

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.280
But soon, Catherine starts to get all sweet on my boy, and they start chillin on the reg.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.579
Hindley still got beef, though — 'specially since Earnshaw favors Heathcliff.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:01.240
When Earnshaw checks out for good, Hindley puts Heathcliff in his place and makes him work like a slave.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.820
Unacceptable!

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:06.920
Everything’s bumpin til Heathcliff’s biddy meets Edgar from T-cross Grange,

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.040
who starts cockblocking our boy by layin the mack on Catherine.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.980
Since Edgar’s pants saggin from them $100 bills, and Heathcliff broke as sh*t,

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.800
Catherine decide she gonna marry Edgar, even though she don’t love him.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.700
Skank!

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:26.460
But Heathcliff be all like, “Naw, f**k this! I’m out,” and chunks deuce outta Wuthering Heights.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.620
Years later, Heathcliff comes back
minted like a f**kin balla.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.720
Ain’t nobody know where he got dem swole dollas from,

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.040
but he gonna use it to get back at all dem haters who dun sh*t in his cereal.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.480
Heathcliff swindles Hindley and his son Hareton, jacks Wuthering Heights,

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.980
and treats Hindley like a b*tch til
he dies.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.640
Then, he marries Edgar’s sister, Isabella, just to get his hands on T-Grange.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:55.340
After Catherine dies birthin a little baby Cathy, Heathcliff’s wife, Isabella, peaces out to London,

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.800
where she gives birth to Heathy’s boy, Linton.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.740
10 years later, Baby Cathy still livin in T-Grange, and Heathcliff got his boy, Linton, back.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.520
When Linton starts hollerin at Cathy, Heathcliff forces them to marry,

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.380
so he can get his grubby hands on T- Grange.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.460
After Linton dies, Heathcliff got it all and
keeps Cathy under lockdown.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:21.460
After a lot of time and choice words, Cathy warms up to Hindley’s son, Hareton, and they get engaged.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.700
But Heathcliff ain’t never gonna see that day,

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:32.340
cuz Catherine’s memory haunts Heathcliff so raw that it kills him.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:38.020
Dub Hizzy is a trill example about what happens when a playa's soul is torn between love and hate.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.000
Heathcliff spends the first half of the book tryna hang on to his hunny, Catherine,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.000
all while gettin smacked around by Hindley.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.680
But once Catherine marries Edgar, Heathcliff feels like he got played and starts sippin that haterade.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.760
But Heathcliff ain’t bringin his
vengeance to the streets.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:56.400
To wreck these rich haters, Heathcliff gotta beat them at they own game.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.140
He gets the jump on Hindley by stackin grands and swiping his hood;

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:03.580
then, he uses his own wife and kids to get more green.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:07.600
And so for Heathcliff, his wife and kids are just another commodity to trade.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:13.020
But it ain’t enough to just burn all his back-when brothas, he also gotta mess with da new kids on the block.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.200
And the next generation always ends up mirroring the last.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:22.260
Just like Heathcliff caught beatdowns from Hindley left and right, Heathcliff wrecks Hareton 24/7.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.140
But no matter how lost Heathcliff gets lookin for vengeance,

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.720
he’ll always be haunted by the woman he loves.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.140
In fact, he got exactly what he wanted:

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.160
“Catherine Earnshaw, may you not rest as long as I am living;

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:41.200
you said I killed you — haunt me, then! ... Be with me always — take any form — drive me mad!

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.340
Only do not leave me in this abyss, where I cannot find you!"

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.260
Peep this symbol, son. Catherine’s
love can go one of two ways.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.960
Wuthering Heights is surrounded by
a whole bunch of nature and crazy weather,

00:03:52.969 --> 00:03:56.715
representin the hard core passion of Catherine’s love for Heathy.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.860
T-Grange, on the other hand, is all clean and sheltered,

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.480
which reppin the easy livin of Catherine’s marriage to the hood-rich Edgar.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.420
When Catherine makes her choice, so does Heathcliff —&nbsp;revenge.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:11.840
And while love don’t conquer all in no simple way, it eventually wins out.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.020
Heathcliff drops his venemous revenge after seeing Hareton and Cathy gettin fresh,

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.180
cuz they be reminding him of Catherine.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.760
And since he reclaims his humanity
by dropping his vengeful grind,

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:27.580
H-Dog’s departed soul can finally join the ghost of Catherine that's been hauntin him for so long.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:31.640
When Nelly peeps a scared boy
crying and asks him what’s wrong, he say,

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:36.920
“There’s Heathcliff and a woman yonder, under t’nab,’... I darnut pass ‘em.”

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.020
Thanks for tunin in, my well-read
thugs! Stay smart, and stay in school!

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:42.520
Peace!

